# Full ERA Prompt Text
prompt: |
  We have up until now done experiments with two major types of codes, that are described in detail below. We also have created a hybrid model that performs well on a short period of time. PLEASE MODIFY THE ALGORITHM THAT USES THE BEST PARTS OF BOTH STRATEGIES TO CREATE A HYBRID STRATEGY THAT IS TRULY WONDERFUL AND SCORES HIGHER THAN EITHER OF THE INDIVIDUAL STRATEGIES ON THE ENTIRE SEASON.
  
  Code 1: Climatological Model
  - Non-parametric, historical quantile lookup.
  - Explicit seasonal focus (week of year).
  - Geo-specific and geo-aggregated ensemble.
  - Rate-based normalization.
  
  Code 2: Autoregressive (AR) Model
  - Parametric, time-series forecasting (AR(6)).
  - Autocorrelation focus (lags).
  - Shared AR parameters across locations, location-specific error variances.
  - Fourth-root data transformation.
